$ golem-launcher plugin add
-- stderr --
error: plugin add takes exactly one argument

Usage: golem-launcher plugin add <path>[@version]

Adds a plugin to launcher.json. Without a version the latest release tag
(go's module query @latest) is looked up and written pinned. A local module
directory (./dir) is written as it is. Adding a listed plugin with a version
changes its version. launcher.json is written only if the result builds.

Example:
  golem-launcher plugin add github.com/golem-mc/essentials
  golem-launcher plugin add github.com/golem-mc/essentials@v1.3.0
  golem-launcher plugin add ./my-plugin

Flags on every command:
  -config file   the launcher's configuration (default launcher.json)
  -cache dir     where toolchains, releases and builds are kept
                 (default: the user cache directory + /golem)
  -color when    colour and progress bars: auto, always or never (default
                 auto: on a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set; FORCE_COLOR
                 forces colour)
-- exit: 2 --

